\description{
The Interference measurement model for change detection by Lin and Oberauer (2022). The observer retrieves a feature
from the retrieval distribution of \code{\link[=imm]{imm()}} and compares it with the probe:
"change" is answered when the retrieved feature is unlikely under the
hypothesis that the probe is the stored item (Lin & Oberauer, 2022, Eq. 8).
The memory parameters are those of \code{\link[=imm]{imm()}}, so the versions \code{full}, \code{bsc}
and \code{abc} and \code{variable_precision} are the same; the decision adds the
criterion.
